From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: emuTOS-MCD <darekadumon@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 09:12:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 143/185] Stop resetting the decoder on every read

D: reads on the console. The round that did it also says what it cost:
71 seeks against 11 waits, and 13,018 sectors rejected by the mode gate
against 651 accepted. Ninety-five per cent chaff, and a seek for almost
every sector delivered.

cd_fetch() called cdc_setup() at the top of every read, and cdc_setup()
is a full CDC reset -- register $F, then IFCTRL, WA, PT and the control
pair. Sega does not do that: CDCSTART initialises the decoder once and
ROMREADN streams from it afterwards. A decoder that has just been reset
has to re-acquire sync, and everything it emits while doing so is
chaff, so 71 resets buy 71 bursts of it -- and the loop closes on
itself, because chaff means no ring entry, which means a timeout, which
means another seek and another reset.

Initialise it when it is not up, and leave it alone when it is. A seek
does not require the decoder to be torn down; the sectors after one are
the same sectors from a new place. cdc_stop() clears the flag, so a
genuine teardown still gets a genuine setup.

This cannot be measured in the emulator -- gpgx does not model sync
acquisition, so its decoder never produces chaff and its boot probe
costs the same four seeks either way. Verified there only as no
regression: D: still mounts, cd_why 0, cd_dtest 3. The numbers that
decide it are seek against wait, and mode against v11, on hardware.

Also retired: the STAT0 bit 7 experiment. Its own criterion was that
v10 and v01 both come back near zero. The console says v11 651, v10
348, v01 31 -- bit 7 predicts a good mode byte 97% of the time, but 348
sectors carry the flag with a bad mode byte and 31 carry a good mode
byte without it. Gating on it would drop 5% of the good sectors to save
work on chaff that should not be there in the first place. The gate
stays out.
---
 bios/scdapi.h |  2 +-
 bios/segacd.c | 24 ++++++++++++++++++++++--
 2 files changed, 23 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/bios/scdapi.h b/bios/scdapi.h
index 174683a..d44878c 100644
--- a/bios/scdapi.h
+++ b/bios/scdapi.h
@@ -28,7 +28,7 @@
 #define SCDAPI_H
 
 #define SCD_COOKIE   0x53674344L        /* 'SgCD' */
-#define SCD_VERSION  11
+#define SCD_VERSION  12
 
 /* Everything the disc diagnostic prints, in one go. Taken in a single
  * call rather than twenty accessors so that the numbers in one report
diff --git a/bios/segacd.c b/bios/segacd.c
index 8990254..1cca856 100644
--- a/bios/segacd.c
+++ b/bios/segacd.c
@@ -1258,7 +1258,21 @@ const UBYTE cdc_ladder[3][2] = {
  * this driver has always written. A first read attempt therefore
  * behaves exactly as it did before, and only a failed one escalates. */
 UBYTE cdc_rung = 2;
-static UBYTE cdc_rung_ok;       /* this rung put a sector in the ring */
+static UBYTE cdc_rung_ok;
+/* The decoder is initialised and has not been torn down since.
+ *
+ * cdc_setup() is a full CDC reset -- register $F, then IFCTRL, WA, PT
+ * and the control pair -- and cd_fetch() called it at the top of every
+ * read. Sega does not: CDCSTART initialises the decoder once and
+ * ROMREADN streams from it thereafter. The console's own counters show
+ * what the difference costs. The round that finally read this disc
+ * reports 71 seeks against 11 waits, and 13,018 sectors rejected by
+ * the mode gate against 651 accepted -- 95% chaff. A decoder that has
+ * just been reset must re-acquire sync and everything it emits while
+ * doing so is chaff, so 71 resets buy 71 bursts of it, and the loop
+ * closes on itself: reset, garbage, no ring entry, timeout, seek,
+ * reset. */
+static UBYTE cdc_live;       /* this rung put a sector in the ring */
 /* Which rungs have been written since boot, one bit each.
  *
  * The instantaneous rung is close to useless and the first hardware log
@@ -1316,6 +1330,7 @@ static void cdc_setup(void)
         }
         set_sr(sr);
     }
+    cdc_live = 1;
 }
 
 /* CDCSTOP, $1FB6: mask level 5, write IFCTRL twice, and finish by
@@ -1326,6 +1341,7 @@ static void cdc_stop(void)
 
     WORD sr = set_sr(0x2700);
 
+    cdc_live = 0;               /* torn down: the next read initialises */
     GA_INTMASK &= (UBYTE)~0x20;
     *CDC_AR = 0x01; *CDC_DATA = 0x38;
     *CDC_AR = 0x01; *CDC_DATA = 0x3A;
@@ -2335,7 +2351,11 @@ static BOOL cd_fetch(ULONG lba)
             cdc_ints = 0;
             cdc_hit = 0;
             if (attempt == 0) {
-                cdc_setup();
+                /* ...and only if it needs it. A seek does not require
+                 * the decoder to be torn down: the sectors that arrive
+                 * after one are the same sectors, from a new place. */
+                if (!cdc_live)
+                    cdc_setup();
             } else {
